 """Tonal sign-in through its Auth0 tenant, using the Tonal mobile app's public client.
 
 Tonal has no developer OAuth: its Auth0 client only accepts the app's own redirect URI,
-so the browser connect flow can't work. A connection is created once with the
-password or email-code grant (see connect.py) and kept alive with the refresh token.
+so the provider's login page can't be used. Instead the "authorization URL" is our own
+sign-in form (signin.py). It signs in with the password or email-code grant, parks the
+tokens in Redis under a one-time code, and redirects to Open Wearables' normal callback
+with that code, which _exchange_token redeems. The rest is the standard OAuth path.
+connect.py does the same from a terminal.
+
 Tonal's API takes the Auth0 *id_token* as its bearer, so that is what we store as the
 access token.
 """
 
